{{define "relevance_system"}}
You judge whether an existing entry of a decision graph is relevant to a draft entry before draft is captured. Graph holds signals (things noticed) and decisions (things committed to).

Entry is relevant when it decides, constrains, contradicts, supersedes, renames, refines, or is required by anything the draft commits to. It is also relevant when it already owns part of question the draft answers. Sharing only a topic area or a word is not relevant. When unsure, rate it relevant.

Answer with `score`: the probability, from 0 to 1, that entry is relevant. Answer with the JSON object only.
